WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.965 --> 00:00:19.007
think our history teacher is actually making history," Jonathan joked to Carlos.

2
00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:22.688
They were walking down the school hallway on Wednesday afternoon.

3
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.710
the most boring teacher ever!"

4
00:00:28.431 --> 00:00:29.171
Carlos nodded.

5
00:00:29.191 --> 00:00:31.772
"I almost fell asleep in class today."

6
00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:34.336
"Me too," Jonathan said.

7
00:00:34.356 --> 00:00:37.457
"And I almost threw up my lunch from the school cafeteria.

8
00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:42.439
If I suddenly fall down dead, blame that weird-smelling cheese-and-bean thing I ate."

9
00:00:43.519 --> 00:00:44.259
Carlos grinned.

10
00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:46.920
"Okay. Just don't throw up on me!"

11
00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.421
"I'll try not to," Jonathan said, laughing.

12
00:00:50.441 --> 00:00:52.021
"What a lousy day."

13
00:00:52.041 --> 00:00:55.322
"Look on the bright side," Carlos pointed out.

14
00:00:55.342 --> 00:00:57.303
"School's over for the day.

15
00:00:57.983 --> 00:00:59.343
Things can only get better for you."

16
00:00:59.363 --> 00:01:02.144
"Hey, guys," someone behind them said.

17
00:01:03.944 --> 00:01:05.424
Jonathan and Carlos turned around.

18
00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:08.865
Things had only gotten worse, not better.

19
00:01:09.726 --> 00:01:12.586
Max was walking down the hallway behind them, carrying a soccer ball.

20
00:01:12.606 --> 00:01:17.548
"Hey, Max," Jonathan muttered.

21
00:01:18.208 --> 00:01:18.928
Carlos nodded.

22
00:01:19.928 --> 00:01:21.089
"Hey. How's it going?"

23
00:01:21.109 --> 00:01:26.630
"Good. I'm going to practice my soccer skills at the park across the street," Max said.

24
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:29.191
"Do you guys want to kick the ball around with me?"

25
00:01:29.211 --> 00:01:31.891
"Sure," Carlos said.

26
00:01:31.911 --> 00:01:33.672
"Will your dad be there?"

27
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:34.821
Jonathan asked.

28
00:01:35.841 --> 00:01:36.622
Max shook his head.

29
00:01:36.642 --> 00:01:39.063
"Nope." That was a relief.

30
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:43.345
In Jonathan's opinion, the only person worse than Max was Max's dad.

31
00:01:43.365 --> 00:01:46.367
"Okay," Jonathan said.

32
00:01:47.168 --> 00:01:47.968
Carlos was going.

33
00:01:49.029 --> 00:01:51.950
And Jonathan figured that he could leave the park if Max got too annoying.

34
00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.772
"Great!" Max sounded surprisingly friendly.

35
00:01:56.573 --> 00:01:58.494
Max surprised Jonathan again at the park.

36
00:01:59.535 --> 00:02:01.676
He took turns kicking the ball with Jonathan and Carlos.

37
00:02:04.768 --> 00:02:08.389
And he didn't brag about being a better player than they were, though clearly he was.

38
00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:12.830
While they practiced soccer passes, Jonathan told one of his favorite jokes.

39
00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:14.131
"Hey, Max.

40
00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:16.912
Why did Cinderella get chosen last for the soccer team?"

41
00:02:16.932 --> 00:02:19.452
"Huh?" Max said.

42
00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.113
"I have no idea."

43
00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:23.334
"Because she ran away from the ball!"

44
00:02:24.354 --> 00:02:25.134
Jonathan laughed.

45
00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:29.655
Carlos laughed too, even though he'd heard the joke a million times before.

46
00:02:30.336 --> 00:02:31.376
But Max just shrugged.

47
00:02:33.076 --> 00:02:35.758
"Max really has no sense of humor," Jonathan thought.

48
00:02:36.579 --> 00:02:38.100
It wasn't the first time he'd noticed this.

49
00:02:39.241 --> 00:02:41.363
But other than that, Max seemed pretty cool today.

50
00:02:41.383 --> 00:02:44.505
"Have you seen Lionel Messi do this double fake?"

51
00:02:45.086 --> 00:02:45.686
Max asked.

52
00:02:46.447 --> 00:02:47.768
He stopped the ball between his feet.

53
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.712
Then he lifted his right foot and took a quick step to the right.

54
00:02:53.613 --> 00:02:55.054
But he dribbled the ball to the left.

55
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:00.538
one!" Carlos said.

56
00:03:00.558 --> 00:03:02.660
"I see why it's called a double fake.

57
00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:06.510
You lift your foot and step the opposite way from where you're really going."

58
00:03:07.811 --> 00:03:08.392
Max nodded.

59
00:03:08.412 --> 00:03:12.675
"Right." "That's a cool move," Carlos said.

60
00:03:12.695 --> 00:03:16.217
"When Messi does it, it's amazing.

61
00:03:17.058 --> 00:03:22.061
I'll never be as good as he is, but I definitely like practicing his moves," Max said.

62
00:03:22.081 --> 00:03:25.423
"And maybe I can get a soccer scholarship for college."

63
00:03:26.524 --> 00:03:28.566
Jonathan tried the double fake, but he couldn't do it.

64
00:03:31.548 --> 00:03:33.713
"Max, can you show us that in slow motion?"

65
00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:34.594
he asked.

66
00:03:35.694 --> 00:03:38.356
"Sure." Max demonstrated the double fake again.

67
00:03:41.918 --> 00:03:43.739
Then he helped Jonathan and Carlos practice it.

68
00:03:43.759 --> 00:03:46.801
"This is awesome," Jonathan said.

69
00:03:47.681 --> 00:03:50.083
It was the first new thing he'd learned since joining his team.

70
00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:53.004
Next Max did what he called the hip fake.

71
00:03:53.705 --> 00:03:57.407
He turned his entire body to the right and looked to the right too, as if he'd found

72
00:03:57.447 --> 00:03:58.708
a teammate to pass the ball to.

73
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.422
Then he quickly turned his body to the left and kicked the ball left.

74
00:04:06.526 --> 00:04:08.668
have a ton of talent," Carlos said.

75
00:04:08.688 --> 00:04:12.771
"Thanks, but really I just work hard," Max said.

76
00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:16.194
"Max is so different today," Jonathan thought.

77
00:04:16.935 --> 00:04:20.718
It was as if a nice, humble space alien had secretly taken over Max's body.

78
00:04:21.899 --> 00:04:24.541
Or maybe Max acted like a jerk only when his father was around.

79
00:04:25.582 --> 00:04:26.443
Jonathan looked at him.

80
00:04:26.463 --> 00:04:27.644
"Hey, Max.

81
00:04:28.428 --> 00:04:29.989
Do you like having your dad coach you?"

82
00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:30.950
he asked.

83
00:04:32.111 --> 00:04:32.792
Max frowned.

84
00:04:33.633 --> 00:04:35.454
"He definitely helps me improve my game."

85
00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:39.878
"I wish he'd help everyone improve their game," Jonathan blurted out.

86
00:04:39.898 --> 00:04:43.041
"But we can't improve if we pass the ball to you all the time.

87
00:04:44.021 --> 00:04:46.804
Why don't you ask your dad to let the rest of the team have the ball more?"

88
00:04:48.545 --> 00:04:49.586
Max crossed his arms.

89
00:04:49.606 --> 00:04:52.529
"My father is the coach and he makes the rules.

90
00:04:53.349 --> 00:04:56.252
Instead of complaining, you should take soccer more seriously and practice more."

91
00:04:57.384 --> 00:04:58.745
Jonathan crossed his arms too.

92
00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:01.087
"Practice passing the ball to you?

93
00:05:01.908 --> 00:05:02.468
No thanks."

94
00:05:02.488 --> 00:05:06.752
"Uh Carlos looked from Jonathan to Max.

95
00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:09.174
"We should probably go, Jonathan.

96
00:05:09.935 --> 00:05:10.715
See you later, Max."

97
00:05:10.735 --> 00:05:14.558
"Bye," Max said, dribbling the ball away from them.

98
00:05:17.521 --> 00:05:20.303
Jonathan didn't say anything until he and Carlos were outside the park.

99
00:05:20.323 --> 00:05:21.925
"That kid's a jerk."

100
00:05:23.086 --> 00:05:23.846
Carlos shrugged.

101
00:05:24.607 --> 00:05:25.748
"He's really good at soccer.

102
00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.302
Maybe you shouldn't say stuff about his dad."

103
00:05:28.322 --> 00:05:31.964
"Yeah, but Jonathan was suddenly sick of soccer.

104
00:05:32.685 --> 00:05:33.586
He dropped the subject.

105
00:05:33.606 --> 00:05:35.527
"See you tomorrow, Carlos."

106
00:05:36.888 --> 00:05:41.371
When Jonathan turned onto his street a few minutes later, he saw Andrew and Aaron shooting a basketball

107
00:05:41.431 --> 00:05:42.692
into the hoop on their driveway.

108
00:05:46.115 --> 00:05:47.896
At least they were trying to shoot the ball into the hoop.

109
00:05:48.617 --> 00:05:50.518
They were much better at soccer than basketball.

110
00:05:51.619 --> 00:05:52.460
Jonathan joined in.

111
00:05:57.088 --> 00:06:00.229
He wasn't very good at basketball either, but he liked fooling around with the ball.

112
00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:01.710
"What's new?"

113
00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.291
Andrew asked as he dribbled the ball up the driveway.

114
00:06:04.311 --> 00:06:06.972
"I just hung out with Max Wattenbarger.

115
00:06:07.732 --> 00:06:09.813
Now I'm in a bad mood," Jonathan said.

116
00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:12.594
"That would put me in a bad mood too."

117
00:06:13.235 --> 00:06:15.936
Andrew took a shot, and the basketball went through the hoop.

118
00:06:19.617 --> 00:06:20.738
Jonathan scooped up the ball.

119
00:06:20.758 --> 00:06:23.579
"You should play pro basketball.

120
00:06:24.419 --> 00:06:26.260
You could be the next LeBron James, Andrew!"

121
00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:27.193
he joked.

122
00:06:27.213 --> 00:06:29.514
"I'm a lot better at soccer.

123
00:06:30.255 --> 00:06:33.017
But I'm still glad we quit the soccer team," Andrew said.

124
00:06:33.037 --> 00:06:38.542
"What?" Jonathan was so surprised, he dropped the ball.

125
00:06:39.603 --> 00:06:41.084
It rolled down the driveway and into the gutter.

126
00:06:45.027 --> 00:06:48.250
got sick of watching Max hog the ball all the time," Aaron said.

127
00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.772
"So we told Coach we were quitting."

128
00:06:50.792 --> 00:06:53.895
"Wow," Jonathan murmured.

129
00:06:54.535 --> 00:06:55.176
"That's a bummer."

130
00:06:56.236 --> 00:06:58.037
He liked having the twins on his soccer team.

131
00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:01.019
He went to get the ball and then took a shot.

132
00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:04.622
"You should stay on the team.

133
00:07:05.282 --> 00:07:06.143
You're good players.

134
00:07:07.004 --> 00:07:09.605
And if we lose you guys, we won't have any substitutes."

135
00:07:10.706 --> 00:07:12.307
"Sorry," Aaron said.

136
00:07:12.327 --> 00:07:14.108
"We're done with that team."

137
00:07:14.128 --> 00:07:16.650
"Don't you want to still play soccer?"

138
00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:17.671
Jonathan asked.

139
00:07:18.692 --> 00:07:22.134
"The only one who really gets to play is Max Wattenbarger," Andrew said.

140
00:07:22.154 --> 00:07:24.736
"The rest of us just pass the ball to him."

141
00:07:25.876 --> 00:07:27.057
"Yeah. No thanks."

142
00:07:27.758 --> 00:07:29.279
Aaron threw the basketball to Jonathan.

143
00:07:30.441 --> 00:07:33.524
Jonathan was still distracted by thoughts of playing soccer without the twins.

144
00:07:34.424 --> 00:07:36.867
So he didn't notice the approaching basketball until it hit him.

145
00:07:37.607 --> 00:07:39.109
Hard. In his gut.
